BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/read-therapy-dog-209292"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Read to a Therapy Dog!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T110000
UID:827dea07a67145b09ea7b440c6742f31@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Storytime\, Toddlers\, Children\, Tweens\n\nTherap
 y dogs will be at the library twice a month for students and emerging read
 ers to get more comfortable reading out loud in a judgement-free environme
 nt. On the 1st Saturday of each month\, we welcome Mojo an Aussie doodle\,
  and the 3rd Saturday we have 2 of either Brodie\, Brooklyn\, or Jessie\, 
 all from the same owner (medium-sized dogs that look like the image on the
  posters). The 3rd Saturday of the month will have K-Pets volunteers who r
 egister on their own when available. We may get a broad range of dog breed
 s and personalities. Feel free to attend both or opt for just one.Registra
 tion for this program offers you the chance to make sure you get a time sl
 ot. After all registered patrons arrive\, walk-ins will be allowed on the 
 list. Each child will get a 10-minute time slot to start. If you would lik
 e a second slot\, you can get on the waitlist by telling Miss Esther. If t
 here are spots left\, it will be first come first serve.If you can't make 
 it after registering\, please contact Miss Esther at emartin@manheimlibrar
 y.org or call (717)665-6700 Ext. 4200 for the circulation desk so we can t
 ake you off the list and allow everyone a chance.When you arrive\, you wil
 l need a book to read. You have the library at your disposal or you can br
 ing your own. You can start halfway if you want. Read whatever you like!
LOCATION:Manheim Community\, MAN Meeting Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/read-therapy-dog-209292
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
