UID:03c4b7cc4815a9d648137fe10b56cca7@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Discussion\, Teens\n\nTeens are invited on a journey to create
  a personalized Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP). WRAP is an evidence-
 based\, interactive\, psycho-educational course where teens will explore s
 tressors\, early warning signs\, crisis planning and developing their own 
 wellness toolbox. Meals will be provided at 5PMActivities start at 5:30PMT
 his six-week program will be led by Licensed Clinical Social Worker\, Jana
 e Allgire and Master's Level Social Worker\, Ashlee Rineer. Session One: I
 ntro to WrapSession Two: Wellness ToolboxSession Three: My Daily PlanSessi
 on Four: StressorsSession Five: Early Warning Signs & When Things Break Do
 wnSession Six: Crisis & Post-CrisisConsistent attendance is recommended\, 
 but not strictly required.Space is limited · Registration is requiredAges
  14-18This series is made possible by the LGBTQ+ Giving Circle & All Seaso
 ns Wellness LLC.
LOCATION:Lancaster\, LPL Meeting and Media Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/creating-my-wellness-pla
 n-201865
