DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T120000
DTSTAMP:20261114T011402
CREATED:20261109T191014Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T191403Z
UID:38867-1796464800-1796472000@apostlesucc.org
SUMMARY:Holiday Grief Workshop
DESCRIPTION:💙 The holidays can be a difficult time when you’re grieving or learning to navigate life after a loss. This December\, our Inclusive Church focus is grief during the holidays\, and we’re making space for those feelings with a special Holiday Grief Workshop led by Grief & After-Loss Mentor Megan Malick. 🕯️ \nDuring this two-hour workshop\, you’ll create your own 5 Senses First Aid Kit\, using sight\, sound\, scent\, touch\, and taste to help ground your nervous system and find moments of comfort when grief feels overwhelming. \n📅 Saturday\, December 5\, from 10 AM–12 PM at COA.\n💲 Cost: $25 per person (covers workshop materials).\n🎟️ Register through Realm\, by calling or emailing the church office\, or online by Clicking Here \n💚 Scholarships are available to help cover the cost if needed. Please speak with Rev. Kathryn Kuhn for more information.
URL:https://apostlesucc.org/event/holiday-grief-workshop/
LOCATION:Church of the Apostles UCC\, 1850 Marietta Ave\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://apostlesucc.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Holiday-Grief-Workshop-12.5.26-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/read-therapy-dog-210405"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Read to a Therapy Dog!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T110000
UID:43463080cb545eefece1307c8161fd04@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Storytime\, Toddlers\, Children\, Tweens\n\nTherap
 y dogs will be at the library twice a month for students and emerging read
 ers to get more comfortable reading out loud in a judgement-free environme
 nt. On the 1st Saturday of each month\, we welcome MOJO an Aussiedoodle\, 
 and the 3rd Saturday we have 2 of either Brodie\, Brooklyn\, or Jessie\, a
 ll from the same owner (medium-sized dogs that look like the image on the 
 posters). The 3rd Saturday of the month will have K-Pets volunteers who re
 gister on their own when available. We may get a broad range of dog breeds
  and personalities. Feel free to attend both or opt for just one.Registrat
 ion for this program offers you the chance to make sure you get a time slo
 t. After all registered patrons arrive\, walk-ins will be allowed on the l
 ist. Each child will get a 10-minute time slot to start. If you would like
  a second slot\, you can get on the waitlist by telling Miss Esther. If th
 ere are spots left\, it will be first come first serve.If you can't make i
 t after registering\, please contact Miss Esther at emartin@manheimlibrary
 .org or call (717)665-6700 Ext. 4200 for the circulation desk so we can ta
 ke you off the list and allow everyone a chance.When you arrive\, you will
  need a book to read. You have the library at your disposal or you can bri
 ng your own. You can start halfway if you want. Read whatever you like!
LOCATION:Manheim Community\, MAN Meeting Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/read-therapy-dog-210405
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
