X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Starting Arting: Art Appreciation for Kids
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261212T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261212T150000
UID:5b06c3e13c615d8a1ab0a70c20ecca2e@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Arts & Crafts\, Children\n\nAges 5-9Have you ever wondered abo
 ut a beautiful painting you've seen hanging in the library? It's time to l
 earn more about the art that surrounds you every day!Start Arting by learn
 ing the basic concepts of art and seeing how they look in our library gall
 ery and on a famous painting. Then try it for yourself! This program will 
 have a hands-on art project involving paint. Please dress accordingly.This
  month\, we will learn about different types of line - how they create tex
 ture and atmosphere in a piece of art. We will look at the library's Joine
 d at the Heart by Allen Miller hanging in the Lapp Story Silo. We will als
 o venture into Cubism and practice our Pointillism with Georges Seurat's S
 unday Afternoon on the Island of La Grande Jatte. Line up for your spot to
 day!Registration will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, November 25th for Manh
 eim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, December 2nd f
 or residents of other municipalities. Registration Requirements:  Please r
 egister ONLY the children who will be attending. Accompanying Adults –
  This program is for adults and children to enjoy together. Please plan 
 to attend and be engaged with your child. Drop offs will not be permitted.
  No Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for more than 
 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from registering for futu
 re programs for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your registr
 ations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow those o
 n the waiting list to be notified of their change in registration status. 
 Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the
  program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The program will be
 gin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot will be forf
 eited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots remain
 \, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, registrants will
  not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start time. 
 Cancellations- Please check your email prior to departing to verify that t
 he program has not been cancelled. Photography - The Manheim Township Publ
 ic Library Code of Conduct Policy prohibits photographing or video recordi
