DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270115T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270115T170000
UID:8d5fce1542aa162e8458751453e4d915@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Book Club\, Health & Wellness\, Children\n\nAges 4-11\, regist
 ered patrons will be given 15 minute reading slots you may select when reg
 istering.  Walk-ins may be accommodated if slots remain open. We thank eac
 h family for waiting outside the Story Corner until your child's turn. Com
 e read to a dog at Quarryville Library!  Lily and Carly will take turns co
 ming to visit us. They love to hear kids read and won't mind if you stumbl
 e on a word here or there.  Share a story you love with a furry friend\, o
 r consider reading one of their favorite books: Go\, Dog! Go! by PD Eastma
 nNoodle and the No-Bones Day by Jonathan GrazianoCan I Be Your Dog?  by Tr
 oy CummingsHarry the Dirty Dog by Gene ZionWhere's Spot? by Eric HillCliff
 ord the Big Red Dog by Norman BridwellSheep in a Jeep by Nancy ShawThe Lan
 dis family will be coming to our library with one of their dogs (Lily and 
 Carly) once per month and they are excited to listen to your stories. We t
 hank them for volunteering to bring back this youth program!
LOCATION:Quarryville\, QVL Story Corner/Early Literacy Lab
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/sit-stay-read-200772
